[
  {
    "sha": "77f402386fdb50bef1b3527ecfa177799efd8bd1",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDc3ZjQwMjM4NmZkYjUwYmVmMWIzNTI3ZWNmYTE3Nzc5OWVmZDhiZDE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T19:02:36Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T19:02:36Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): recognise pockets and slots and turn them into operations\n\nA new app module, recognize, reads a model's planar-face topology for\nflat floors whose outer ring has walls rising into them on opposite\nsides: closed pockets, open pockets, and straight slots with open,\nround or square ends. Each answer carries the floor's ring, floor and\ntop Z, depth, area, tightest inside corner, open spans, island count\nand, for a slot, its centreline ends, width and length. Degenerate\nfacets never weld; a missing or empty model is refused by name.\n\nrecognize::operation_for maps one onto CreateOperation's inputs: a 2D\nPocket on a pick of the floor face (depths relative to the selection,\nso they follow a moved part), or a Slot along the centreline for a slot\nwith no square closed end. The MCP tool detect_pockets lists them and,\nwith create, adds the operation as one undo step.\n\nThe GUI entry point is #511. Recognised slots inherit #510 (every\ntyped Slot riding its cap is convicted of a gouge today).\n\nFixes #35\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
